NNAAMMEE
     iissoobboooott — Boot code for hybrid ISO/USB images on BIOS-based computers

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     iissoobboooott is used on BIOS-based computers to boot from an ISO image that
     has been written to a USB flash drive or other HDD-like device.  iissoobboooott
     is installed in a ffrreeeebbssdd--bboooott partition with mkimg(1).

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     The El Torito standard for bootable CDs provides a 32KB "System Area" at
     the beginning of an image.  To create an image that is able to be booted
     by the BIOS as either a CD-ROM ("ISO") and as a more HDD-like image (e.g.
     on a USB flash drive) it is necessary to have both a standard El Torito
     boot catalog containing a HDD-style partition table and boot code.
     iissoobboooott is intended to be placed in a GPT partition to allow the system
     to find the standard FreeBSD loader(8) in the ISO filesystem later in the
     image.

BBOOOOTTIINNGG
     iissoobboooott looks for an ISO filesystem image on the device it was booted
     from and seeks to read either the primary FreeBSD loader(8) or kernel
     from there.

